From 4958a87c4ed5e8616254c0a7640e497c1e49fba4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 20:58:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(vehicles): forward predicted boat and horse movement

Java sends vehicle position and paddle state separately from player movement. Bedrock's server-authoritative input expects the vehicle's predicted position, rotation, unique ID, and paddle flags while riding a client-predicted vehicle. Forward those fields and translate vehicle rewinds back into Java vehicle corrections so boats no longer operate on stale player coordinates.

Translate the Bedrock boat origin and yaw in both directions. Bedrock
boat positions include a 0.375-block vertical offset and a 90-degree yaw
offset, which must be removed for Java rendering and restored for
predicted movement. Sending Java positions unchanged drives Geyser's
Java boat underwater and eventually ejects the rider. Keep absolute and
delta updates, rewinds, passenger exits, and local prediction consistent.

Protocol 2193 evidence: Geyser 2.11.3 VanillaEntities boat definitions and
BoatEntity moveAbsoluteRaw at
https://github.com/GeyserMC/Geyser/tree/63a4e2b79b12f0d138777d5fd80176a112b4bd72/core/src/main/java/org/geysermc/geyser/entity
Tests cover regular/chest boat coordinate and rotation round trips and
unchanged non-boat positions.
